# Cursor Rules for FaithForm

## Mandatory Requirement: Pixel-Accurate Skeleton Loading

When designing or redesigning ANY page or subpage in FaithForm:
1. Always create a matching, pixel-accurate `loading.tsx` file (or `<Suspense fallback={<...Skeleton />}>`).
2. The skeleton must mirror the exact layout geometry: same `max-w-*` container, same grid layout (`grid-cols-*`), same card padding, rounded borders, and headers to eliminate Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS).
3. Use `@/components/ui/skeleton` primitives (`Skeleton`, `SkeletonContainer`, `SkeletonText`). Never leave unstyled empty space or jarring layout jumps.
4. Always wrap loading states in `<SkeletonContainer label="...">` to enforce the 180ms anti-flicker grace period (preventing premature flashing on fast navigations) and accessible ARIA attributes (`role="status"`, `aria-busy="true"`, sr-only announcements).
5. Use `<SkeletonText lines={n} />` for realistic paragraph placeholders with natural varying line widths and font leading parity.
